1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,973
Ten kilograms of rice,
plus ten kilograms of rice.

2
00:00:03,973 --> 00:00:05,667
Always twenty kilograms.

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:10,304
Now you push a box with ten newtons,
and a friend pushes with ten newtons

4
00:00:10,304 --> 00:00:11,204
too.

5
00:00:11,164 --> 00:00:15,680
The total push can be twenty newtons,
or zero, or anything between.

6
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:16,580
How?

7
00:00:16,689 --> 00:00:19,427
Aarav met the same puzzle on his bicycle.

8
00:00:19,777 --> 00:00:23,433
He rode three kilometres east,
then four kilometres north.

9
00:00:23,433 --> 00:00:25,217
His trip meter says seven.

10
00:00:25,617 --> 00:00:28,886
But he is only five kilometres
from the college gate.

11
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:30,661
Three plus four makes five?

12
00:00:30,661 --> 00:00:31,716
Let's find out.

13
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:34,680
Some quantities need only a size.

14
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,257
We call them scalars.

15
00:00:36,607 --> 00:00:38,845
Mass, time, temperature, distance.

16
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:41,353
A number and a unit tell the full story.

17
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:44,534
Other quantities need
a size and a direction.

18
00:00:44,534 --> 00:00:45,971
We call them vectors.

19
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:50,692
Displacement, velocity, acceleration
and force are all vectors.

20
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:55,068
And a vector adds by the triangle
law, not like plain numbers.

21
00:00:55,718 --> 00:00:58,867
Let's replay Aarav's ride
on our motion notebook.

22
00:00:59,217 --> 00:01:01,319
He sets off east from the gate.

23
00:01:01,319 --> 00:01:03,109
The distance counter climbs.

24
00:01:03,109 --> 00:01:05,040
One, two, three kilometres.

25
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,597
The violet arrow is his displacement.

26
00:01:07,597 --> 00:01:10,674
It points from the gate
straight to where he is now.

27
00:01:11,074 --> 00:01:12,392
Now he turns north.

28
00:01:12,392 --> 00:01:14,781
The distance keeps climbing, to seven.

29
00:01:15,181 --> 00:01:19,790
Let's replay that turn in slow motion,
and watch only the violet arrow.

30
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:22,692
It swings towards north, and it grows.

31
00:01:22,692 --> 00:01:24,914
But it stops at five, not seven.

32
00:01:25,314 --> 00:01:28,336
On the graph, distance
climbs in a straight line.

33
00:01:28,336 --> 00:01:30,879
Displacement matches it, then bends below.

34
00:01:31,529 --> 00:01:32,958
Freeze at the end.

35
00:01:32,958 --> 00:01:35,220
Leg one, three kilometres east.

36
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,482
Leg two, four kilometres north.

37
00:01:37,982 --> 00:01:42,213
The displacement arrow joins the tail
of the first leg to the head of the

38
00:01:42,213 --> 00:01:43,113
last.

39
00:01:43,378 --> 00:01:45,607
Now the maths, one step at a time.

40
00:01:45,957 --> 00:01:46,857
Step one.

41
00:01:46,809 --> 00:01:50,498
Distance is a scalar, so
it adds like plain numbers.

42
00:01:50,498 --> 00:01:53,002
Three plus four is seven kilometres.

43
00:01:53,752 --> 00:01:54,652
Step two.

44
00:01:54,568 --> 00:01:56,776
The legs meet at a right angle.

45
00:01:56,776 --> 00:02:00,456
The displacement is the longest
side of a right triangle.

46
00:02:01,206 --> 00:02:02,168
Step three.

47
00:02:02,168 --> 00:02:06,507
By Pythagoras, s squared equals
three squared plus four squared.

48
00:02:06,507 --> 00:02:08,870
Nine plus sixteen is twenty five.

49
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,554
Step four.

50
00:02:10,554 --> 00:02:15,739
So s is five kilometres, pointing about
fifty three degrees north of east.

51
00:02:16,489 --> 00:02:17,616
Remember this.

52
00:02:17,616 --> 00:02:19,827
Scalars add like plain numbers.

53
00:02:19,827 --> 00:02:22,154
Vectors add by the triangle law.

54
00:02:22,854 --> 00:02:24,074
Side by side.

55
00:02:24,074 --> 00:02:28,354
Ten kilograms plus ten kilograms
is always twenty kilograms.

56
00:02:28,754 --> 00:02:33,055
Ten newtons plus ten newtons, pushing
the same way, gives twenty newtons.

57
00:02:33,455 --> 00:02:36,164
At a right angle, about fourteen newtons.

58
00:02:36,164 --> 00:02:38,374
Pushing against each other, zero.

59
00:02:38,774 --> 00:02:40,900
Same numbers, different answers.

60
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,386
The direction decides.

61
00:02:42,886 --> 00:02:43,955
Now you try.

62
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,904
Two pushes of ten newtons act on one box.

63
00:02:46,904 --> 00:02:48,939
Can the total push be zero?

64
00:02:48,939 --> 00:02:50,268
Pause and decide.

65
00:02:53,468 --> 00:02:54,368
Yes!

66
00:02:53,961 --> 00:02:57,876
When the two pushes point in
opposite directions, they cancel.

67
00:02:57,876 --> 00:02:59,520
Mass can never do that.

68
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:02,897
So is a new quantity a scalar or a vector?

69
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:04,080
Follow the links.

70
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:07,276
Speed equals distance divided by time.

71
00:03:07,676 --> 00:03:09,260
Distance is a scalar.

72
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,638
Time is a scalar.

73
00:03:10,638 --> 00:03:13,559
A scalar divided by a scalar is a scalar.

74
00:03:13,559 --> 00:03:15,205
So speed is a scalar.

75
00:03:15,705 --> 00:03:19,061
Velocity equals displacement
divided by time.

76
00:03:19,461 --> 00:03:21,316
Displacement is a vector.

77
00:03:21,316 --> 00:03:25,410
Dividing by time, a positive
number, keeps its direction.

78
00:03:25,410 --> 00:03:27,276
So velocity is a vector.

79
00:03:27,926 --> 00:03:29,034
One more rule.

80
00:03:29,034 --> 00:03:33,429
Two vectors are equal only with the
same size and the same direction.

81
00:03:33,829 --> 00:03:37,563
Move an arrow without turning it,
and it is still the same vector.

82
00:03:37,963 --> 00:03:42,448
But five kilometres east and five
kilometres north are not equal.

83
00:03:42,948 --> 00:03:43,848
Your turn.

84
00:03:43,813 --> 00:03:48,614
Can the size of the displacement ever
be bigger than the distance travelled?

85
00:03:48,614 --> 00:03:49,887
Pause and decide.

86
00:03:53,087 --> 00:03:53,987
No!

87
00:03:53,529 --> 00:03:55,951
A straight line is the shortest path.

88
00:03:55,951 --> 00:03:59,402
So displacement can equal
distance, but never beat it.

89
00:04:00,052 --> 00:04:01,788
Now, one worked example.

90
00:04:02,138 --> 00:04:05,805
A student walks eight metres
east, then six metres north.

91
00:04:05,805 --> 00:04:08,276
Find the distance and the displacement.

92
00:04:08,776 --> 00:04:10,369
Distance is a scalar.

93
00:04:10,369 --> 00:04:12,758
Eight plus six is fourteen metres.

94
00:04:13,508 --> 00:04:15,205
Displacement is a vector.

95
00:04:15,205 --> 00:04:19,583
The legs meet at a right angle, so
s squared equals eight squared plus

96
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:20,529
six squared.

97
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:25,067
That is sixty four plus thirty
six, which is one hundred.

98
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:26,539
So s is ten metres.

99
00:04:27,289 --> 00:04:29,055
Distance, fourteen metres.

100
00:04:29,055 --> 00:04:32,259
Displacement, ten metres,
pointing north of east.

101
00:04:32,909 --> 00:04:34,375
Now, the exam trap.

102
00:04:34,725 --> 00:04:38,221
Aarav rides two kilometres
to college, and back home.

103
00:04:38,221 --> 00:04:40,809
Many students say his distance is zero.

104
00:04:41,159 --> 00:04:42,059
Wrong.

105
00:04:41,753 --> 00:04:43,847
The distance is four kilometres.

106
00:04:43,847 --> 00:04:48,356
It is the displacement that is zero,
because he ends where he started.

107
00:04:49,006 --> 00:04:50,323
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:50,323 --> 00:04:54,222
As quick questions: pick the vector,
or find distance and displacement

109
00:04:54,222 --> 00:04:55,122
for a path.

110
00:04:55,689 --> 00:04:56,890
Exam level now.

111
00:04:56,890 --> 00:05:01,962
A particle moves six metres east, eight
metres north, then six metres west.

112
00:05:01,962 --> 00:05:05,628
Find the ratio of distance
to the size of displacement.

113
00:05:05,628 --> 00:05:06,880
Pause and solve.

114
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,718
The answer is A.

115
00:05:13,718 --> 00:05:14,865
Five to two.

116
00:05:15,365 --> 00:05:19,138
Distance is six plus eight plus
six, which is twenty metres.

117
00:05:19,638 --> 00:05:21,143
East and west cancel.

118
00:05:21,143 --> 00:05:23,850
So the displacement is eight metres north.

119
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:27,271
Twenty divided by eight is five over two.

120
00:05:27,271 --> 00:05:28,353
Five to two.

121
00:05:28,853 --> 00:05:30,312
Here is your recap.

122
00:05:30,312 --> 00:05:31,812
Screenshot this card.

123
00:05:35,012 --> 00:05:37,849
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

124
00:05:38,249 --> 00:05:39,149
One.

125
00:05:38,768 --> 00:05:41,966
How can ten newtons plus
ten newtons give zero?

126
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:43,766
Two.

127
00:05:43,361 --> 00:05:46,114
Is speed a scalar or a vector, and why?

128
00:05:47,014 --> 00:05:47,914
Three.

129
00:05:47,611 --> 00:05:50,520
Can displacement ever
be bigger than distance?

130
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:56,169
Next time: how do you draw a vector
so that anyone can read its size and

131
00:05:56,169 --> 00:05:57,203
its direction?

132
00:05:57,203 --> 00:05:59,578
We find out in vector representation.
